vent_uuid":"72c592c7-d2b8-4d05-a55f-86e0a9242396","position":{"commit_sha":"403ee3c1041f1667a6822573e93be058361b79fc","position":"1786561284519193512-72c592c7-d2b8-4d05-a55f-86e0a9242396"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d645d73c6d509d9be4cef02627627cee6952fd6e854b66d761dba6b7cc25e794","event_uuid":"f5910ae0-304e-473f-a784-cf0ee3f91137","position":{"commit_sha":"a77a3519215f77824a5214a339b4fed4e115e3f7","position":"1786563587275463001-f5910ae0-304e-473f-a784-cf0ee3f91137"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"61ff1f16179352cc1cdbd3f304ef6837c4e6147161e537e99b217ed1f36aafad","event_uuid":"8947cf5f-4871-4d1d-a40c-ec54f6871822","position":{"commit_sha":"29383fb2075d2e3fcdb482ee4e86c41acc280685","position":"1786563609918447001-8947cf5f-4871-4d1d-a40c-ec54f6871822"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Split implemented in worktree flamingo-reflock-split.\n\nShape: tail cluster moved to src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock_push.py (147 LOC) via lazy_load('rebar_reconciler_ref_lock_push', '_ref_lock_push.py'). _ref_lock.py: 800 -> 730 LOC. Lines 1-708 are BYTE-IDENTICAL to the pre-split file; only the tail is replaced by four wrapper/binding lines plus the three 4/5-arg wrappers. The call sites at :393, :422, :476 are unchanged.\n\nLate binding: every child entry point takes the calling module as an explicit 'core' first argument and reads core._git / core._REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS / core.logger at CALL time. No import cycle; the child imports nothing from the package.\n\nMutation-checked the new tests rather than trusting them:\n- Mutant (child re-loads _ref_lock under its own loader key — the exact trap the ticket recorded): 13 failures, including all three new patch-point params, the new logger test, and the ticket's recorded symptoms test_transport_failures_stay_fail_closed[auth failed]/[dns failure] and test_cas_mismatch_logs_the_stderr_that_justified_it. Reproduces the previous attempt's failure signature exactly.\n- Mutant (logger re-homed onto the child module): the new logger test fails on record.name == 'rebar_reconciler_ref_lock_push'.\n\nBehaviour-identical note: the two bug-ebee markers that were appended with '+=' are now inline members of the NON_CAS_REJECT_MARKERS tuple literal. Same six values, same order, no semantic change — the '+=' only existed to avoid adding a line under the old cap.\n\nGates so far: 2409 reconciler tests pass; targeted classification + module-size contract pass (23); make lint clean; make typecheck clean (510 files). Full unit suite + complexity ratchet running.","timestamp":1786559767738424001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed as Gerrit change 1668 (commit a4b8e9d0592, branch flamingo-reflock-split): https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1668\n\nFull gate results before push:\n- full unit suite: 9663 passed, 42 skipped\n- reconciler suite: 2409 passed\n- targeted (classification + module-size contract): 23 passed\n- make lint: clean\n- make typecheck: clean, 510 source files\n- complexity ratchet: active=61 new=0 increased=0 stale=0\n- pre-commit hook chain (lint, typecheck, 50/72 commit-message wrap): all passed\n\nSizes against the checked-in .github/module-size-limit.txt of 800:\n- _ref_lock.py 730 (70 lines of margin, was 0)\n- _ref_lock_push.py 147 (over the 100 floor)\n\nAwaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1786560926144126001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LANDED. Gerrit change 1668 MERGED at 2026-08-12 19:39:06 UTC, LLM-Review +1 (PASS, 2 advisory non-blocking, zero inline comments) and Verified +1. Gerrit rebased server-side, so it landed as 0eecf17cd6 rather than the pushed a4b8e9d0592.\n\nVerified against the merged tree (worktree reset to gerrit/main 0eecf17cd6): _ref_lock.py 730 LOC, _ref_lock_push.py 147 LOC, and the 23 targeted tests (push classification + module size contract) pass.\n\nAll 10 ACs met. The margin the ticket existed to restore: _ref_lock.py went from 0 lines of headroom to 70.\n\nNote for whoever picks up the next module-size ticket: src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py is now the file sitting at exactly 800, i.e. it is in precisely the state this ticket was filed about. Worth a ticket of its own before someone hits it mid-fix.","timestamp":1786563609918447001}],"created_at":1786528695909395001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4a6b3daf-7037-4466-aa30-195451ff02ab","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ebee-e959-8015-4e02"},{"link_uuid":"72c592c7-d2b8-4d05-a55f-86e0a9242396","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"36f3-16de-d239-4af5"}],"description":"# Split `_ref_lock.py` — it is pinned at exactly the 800-LOC hard cap\n\n## Why this exists\n\nDiscovered while fixing bug `freeborn-dizzy-raven` (ebee-e959-8015-4e02), whose fix added two\nmarkers to `_NON_CAS_REJECT_MARKERS` in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py`. The\nfile was at 799 lines and the CI module-size gate hard-fails any `src/rebar` file over 800 (no\nallowlist), so a two-line change did not fit. The fix landed by appending the markers in one\n`+=` statement, leaving the file at **exactly 800**. That is a spent margin: the next change to\nthis module, of any size, cannot land without splitting it first.\n\n## Two traps that sank a previous attempt (recorded, not hypothetical)\n\n1. **`rebar._engine` is not an importable package.** `from rebar._engine.rebar_reconciler.X\n   import ...` fails at collection with `ModuleNotFoundError`. Reconciler modules load siblings\n   through the `_loader.py` `lazy_load(<key>, \"<file>.py\")` seam (`_ref_lock` already pulls\n   `_advisory_lock` that way). Any split MUST go through that seam.\n2. **Tests bind to module identity.**\n   `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock_push_classification.py` does\n   `monkeypatch.setattr(_ref_lock, \"_git\", ...)` and then calls\n   `_ref_lock._push_lease_cas(...)`. Two loader keys mean two module objects, so a naively\n   moved `_push_lease_cas` resolves `_git` from the child module and the patch misses. Its\n   `caplog` assertions then fail too — same root cause, not an independent logger-name trap\n   (they assert on record *messages*, not logger names). Keep the log emitting on the\n   `rebar_reconciler._ref_lock` logger anyway, so operator-facing evidence is unchanged.\n\n## Seam\n\nMove the tail cluster (currently lines ~709-800, ~92 LOC) to a sibling `_ref_lock_push.py`:\n`_PUSH_REJECT_MARKERS`, `_LEASE_MISMATCH_MARKER`, `_NON_CAS_REJECT_MARKERS`,\n`_is_cas_mismatch_stderr`, `_push_lease_cas`, `_push_cas`, `_push_delete_cas`. It is a real\nunit: *decide whether a rejected ref push means the lease moved, and issue the lease pushes\nthat ask the question*. Nothing outside `_ref_lock.py` references these names except the one\ntest above.\n\n### Rewiring — all three moved entry points keep 4/5-arg wrappers in `_ref_lock.py`\n\n`_push_cas` and `_push_delete_cas` are called from code that **stays** in `_ref_lock.py`:\n\n- `_ref_lock.py:393` — `_push_cas(repo_root, ref, oid, _ZERO_OID, remote)` in `acquire`'s `_plant()`\n- `_ref_lock.py:476` — `_push_cas(repo_root, ref, new_oid, old_oid, remote)` in `_cas_advance`'s `_do()`\n- `_ref_lock.py:422` — `_push_delete_cas(repo_root, ref, oid, remote)` in `release`'s `_delete()`\n\nIf those three bare calls are left resolving nothing, the remote acquire/release/advance paths\nraise `NameError`. So the parent does **not** move the names away; it re-binds them. Worked\nexample of the parent side after the split:\n\n```python\n_push = lazy_load(\"rebar_reconciler_ref_lock_push\", \"_ref_lock_push.py\")\n_is_cas_mismatch_stderr = _push.is_cas_mismatch_stderr\n\n\ndef _push_lease_cas(repo_root: Path, ref: str, old_oid: str, remote: str, refspec: str) -> None:\n    _push.push_lease_cas(sys.modules[__name__], repo_root, ref, old_oid, remote, refspec)\n\n\ndef _push_cas(repo_root: Path, ref: str, new_oid: str, old_oid: str, remote: str) -> None:\n    _push_lease_cas(repo_root, ref, old_oid, remote, f\"{new_oid}:{ref}\")\n\n\ndef _push_delete_cas(repo_root: Path, ref: str, old_oid: str, remote: str) -> None:\n    _push_lease_cas(repo_root, ref, old_oid, remote, f\":{ref}\")\n```\n\nConsequences that make this the chosen shape rather than a re-export:\n\n- The three call sites at :393, :422 and :476 are **unchanged** — same names, same arity.\n- The child never imports the parent; the parent hands `sys.modules[__name__]` down as an\n  explicit `core` argument, so there is no import cycle and no second module object.\n- The child reads `core._git`, `core._REMOTE_TIMEOUT_SECS` and `core.logger` at **call time**,\n  so `monkeypatch.setattr(_ref_lock, \"_git\", ...)` is seen, and the CAS verdict still logs on\n  the `rebar_reconciler._ref_lock` logger.\n- Line budget: -92 moved, +~14 wrappers, so `_ref_lock.py` lands near 722.\n\nThe module docstring explaining the CAS-vs-server-fault distinction (the subject of bugs 4afc\nand ebee) carries the new file over the 100-LOC floor.\n\n### Verification of the rewire, in-session\n\n- `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/ -q` — exercises `acquire`/`release`/`renew` over the\n  remote path, so a broken :393/:422/:476 binding fails here rather than in production.\n- `python -c \"from rebar_reconciler import _ref_lock; [getattr(_ref_lock, n) for n in\n  ('_push_cas','_push_delete_cas','_push_lease_cas','_is_cas_mismatch_stderr')]\"` — proves each\n  name is still resolvable at the original module path.\n- `grep -rn --include=*.py \"_push_cas\\|_push_delete_cas\" src` returns only `_ref_lock.py`\n  wrapper definitions/call sites and `_ref_lock_push.py` definitions — no orphan reference.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: `_ref_lock.py` <= 730 LOC (real margin under the 800 cap); `_ref_lock_push.py`\n  >= 100 LOC and under the cap.\n- [x] AC2: `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` passes.\n- [x] AC3: `test_ref_lock_push_classification.py` passes with its behavioural assertions\n  untouched.\n- [x] AC4: a test proves `monkeypatch.setattr(_ref_lock, \"_git\", ...)` still intercepts the\n  moved lease-push functions.\n- [x] AC4b: a test proves the CAS-mismatch verdict still logs on the\n  `rebar_reconciler._ref_lock` logger.\n- [x] AC4c: `_push_cas`, `_push_delete_cas`, `_push_lease_cas` and `_is_cas_mismatch_stderr`\n  are all still resolvable as attributes of `rebar_reconciler._ref_lock`, and the call sites at\n  `_ref_lock.py` :393, :422 and :476 are byte-identical to their pre-split form.\n- [x] AC5: CAS classification contract unchanged — `stale info` stays conclusive, the\n  subtractive veto markers still win, ambiguity still fails closed (bugs 4afc, ebee).\n- [x] AC6: `make lint` passes.\n- [x] AC6b: `make typecheck` passes.\n- [x] AC6c: the complexity ratchet passes with no new debt.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py","reason":"Move the CAS classification + lease-push cluster out through the lazy_load sibling seam so the module drops well under the 800-LOC cap"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock_push_classification.py","reason":"Prove the monkeypatch point and the CAS classification contract survive the split; adjust only logger-name expectations if needed"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","36f3-16de-d239-4af5"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e5aacfa8-1116-4de6-947c-3d463b544653","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6d4f-165e-188c-42a3","ticket_type":"task","title":"Split _ref_lock.py — pinned at exactly the 800-LOC hard cap, so the next change of any size cannot land","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["293d9791-6119-452d-b20b-c81eb22f3eff","4a6b3daf-7037-4466-aa30-195451ff02ab","99ff71ce-0081-4160-be24-e5d9e799a774","6142f658-31ce-45db-ad77-376b87ac4602","7215ea33-3e4e-4a96-93d5-117e2a6bbfe8","29837ecd-2746-4259-bcf8-01d0b376168f","e5aacfa8-1116-4de6-947c-3d463b544653","2e34e4bf-1153-4827-836e-95a1990c4915","d58de209-e1f7-4f63-ac1d-624310a5be04","eb8db256-2903-4ca0-ba20-b6330c45a22e","72c592c7-d2b8-4d05-a55f-86e0a9242396","f5910ae0-304e-473f-a784-cf0ee3f91137","8947cf5f-4871-4d1d-a40c-ec54f6871822"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786563609918447002,"uuid":"fd314d99-c84d-4a97-9893-b0637410e555"}